# Build context is the repo root for BOTH images (see the header comment in
# backend/Dockerfile and frontend/Dockerfile). Docker only reads a
# .dockerignore at the context root — a <subdir>/.dockerignore is silently
# ignored when that subdir is not itself the context. This file is therefore
# the only one that has any effect on either build.
#
# Without it, `COPY backend ./backend` / `COPY frontend ./frontend` vendor
# whatever happens to be in the working tree — a local .env kept for host-mode
# testing, a stale dist/, node_modules — straight into the image. Verified
# during review: a probe file inside backend/ landed at /app/backend/ in the
# built image.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
.git
.gitignore
legacy
docs
.planning
**/*.log
.DS_Store
